export anchor TechnicalManualStyle:
    number: 41
    screen: ProjectDetail
    name: Technical manual
    idea: The project is a section of an equipment manual, with numbered clauses like 4.4.3, boxed spec tables, symbol warning boxes and a condensed uppercase sans.
    base: light
    palette:
        bench: #e9e9e4, the page behind the document sheet
        paper: #ffffff, the document sheet
        black: #141414, text, rules, table header rows and buttons
        grey: #4d4d4d, captions, labels and assignees
        tint: #ededed, table row heads, the nav bar and the log entry
        safetyYellow: #ffd23f, the warning symbol panel and the focus halo
        caution: #fff4cc, the warning box and a focused row
        note: #e6eef8, the note box
        link: #0b4a8f, task and file links
    type:
        A condensed sans, "Arial Narrow", "Helvetica Neue Condensed",
        "Roboto Condensed", "Liberation Sans Narrow", Arial, sans-serif,
        with font-stretch condensed. Sizes are 34px bold uppercase for the
        title, 18px bold uppercase section heads led by a clause number,
        15px body at 1.4 line height, 12px bold uppercase captions and tags
        with wide tracking, and 13px monospace for file names.
    layout:
        The page is one framed document sheet with a 2px black border. A
        header block splits into cells for the boxed B mark and Brightwork,
        a document id strip with doc number, unit, start and due, and the
        operator Mara Okafor. A grey nav bar holds uppercase links and a
        Find field. The title block shows Section 4, the uppercase title
        over a 3px rule, and the Add task and Edit project buttons. Two
        columns follow. The left holds 4.1 Specifications as a gridded spec
        table with a segmented gauge, 4.2 Purpose as clauses 4.2.1 and
        4.2.2, and 4.3 Milestone sequence as a table. The right holds 4.4
        Open tasks with a yellow warning box, 4.5 Reference documents as a
        table, and 4.6 Operator log with a note box, the quote and a reply
        field. A footer strip shows the doc id and page number. Below 820px
        everything is one column.
    spacing: A 4px base. 3 to 7px cell padding, 18px between clauses and a 28px column gap.
    density: High. Two columns of clauses on wide screens.
    corners: Square only.
    borders: A 2px black frame round the document, a 1px black table grid, a 3px rule under the title and dotted rules between task rows.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        ISO style safety symbols. A yellow triangle with an exclamation
        mark heads the warning box and a circled i heads the note box, each
        in its own panel. Tags are boxed uppercase words with a tick for On
        track, a solid square for Done, a triangle for Active, a hollow
        square for Pending and a slashed circle for Blocked.
    focus: A 3px black outline offset 2px with a 6px safety yellow halo.
    tone: Imperative and terse, such as Do not publish the customers page until permission is received.
